{"id": "EUVD-2026-81840", "enisaUuid": "7aa569e5-a49a-3900-b895-1856d8b9b3c6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix mmap_lock leak in irq_work path\n\nstack_map_get_build_id_offset() introduced a per-CPU irq_work to defer\nmmap_read_unlock() from NMI context, and bpf_find_vma() later reused the\nsame mmap_unlock_work. Both callers only check whether the work is busy\nbefore taking mmap_lock, so a nested caller can reuse the slot before the\nfirst caller queues it. Two read locks may then be acquired while only one\ndeferred unlock runs, leaking a read lock and blocking exit_mmap().\n\nReserve the per-CPU slot before mmap_read_trylock(). Use the same wrapper\nin stackmap and bpf_find_vma() so both callers release the reservation on\ntrylock failure. Keep rejecting the slot while the irq_work remains busy.\nRelease it after the irq_work callback unlocks the mm.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6c9daf6097f9b39162b8e736a6ac7caf5ef6fc8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/931f62311c058d79f29548f20943969bb441ce87", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a052ad5edccf5319f50ed955de4368f8318a9f20", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/051f2da26ce377f683b938a3382e0f16d02f3139", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fa9dcacdcdf487f0ffef64bf67622f1caed509f1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90247", "GHSA-m447-wf7w-9qp4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c15bfb5-e88a-3253-8806-6286de6e20f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eac9153f2b584c702cea02c1f1a57d85aa9aea42 <b6c9daf6097f9b39162b8e736a6ac7caf5ef6fc8"}, {"id": "13556e5a-c264-35e5-b11b-c0bf3d51d736", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eac9153f2b584c702cea02c1f1a57d85aa9aea42 <931f62311c058d79f29548f20943969bb441ce87"}, {"id": "1879e6a0-5a39-3975-9a63-b9e71982beef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7f4da875c16f3b8bef0d9ec67528111045bfcd8"}, {"id": "1cd09158-5d47-3975-885e-833183b55f90", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f1838da73cccb238b8be4ef464fce0168dc7ba84"}, {"id": "38b6328c-acb6-3d8d-9dad-f225743c22d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "41e82243-310a-3ed4-a428-ce31c77f48d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "5f80399c-f79e-3b67-98ca-2ed326939c8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "68091fb1-3525-3a43-8c0a-e09be9cbf88c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "6cc49ea6-08b1-3d16-baf7-d0c8fe3ad560", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "808f1fad-303c-3f65-beb4-4b069266b1d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4.7 <5.5"}, {"id": "9a300077-f2ad-3fd5-b036-94fa30e9016b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eac9153f2b584c702cea02c1f1a57d85aa9aea42 <fa9dcacdcdf487f0ffef64bf67622f1caed509f1"}, {"id": "9b17ef54-a507-32d5-bdba-9abbf5515763", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eac9153f2b584c702cea02c1f1a57d85aa9aea42 <a052ad5edccf5319f50ed955de4368f8318a9f20"}, {"id": "ae88b4e8-feb6-3e4a-8b2e-fa1985f5ee5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.19.92 <4.20"}, {"id": "b0e79186-fce8-367b-9e10-ff0fd022ba5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.5"}, {"id": "cc78b2d1-2940-3031-95b6-1154edab07ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eac9153f2b584c702cea02c1f1a57